That Council:

Direct staff to prepare notices of Council's Intention to consider issuance of Temporary Use Permit No.
TUP19-0007 to the City of Langford for the purpose of establishing Eco-Tourism and Recreation uses on the
property located by 3680 Trans-Canada Highway subject to the following terms and conditions:


1.    That the following uses will be permitted for a term of 3 years:


        i.        Assembly;
       ii.        One accessory dwelling unit in conjunction with and in addition to any of the other uses
                  permitted in the subsection;
      iii.        Campsite;
      iv.         Conference and meeting facilities;
       v.         Accessory dormitories;
      vi.         Hotel;
     vii.         Recreational facilities, including but not limited to canoe and rowing club, gymnasiums, physical
                  fitness training;
     viii.        Rental of recreational equipment including, but without limited the generality of the foregoing:
                  bicycles, kayaks and canoes, clothing and outdoor gear;
      ix.         Restaurants;
       x.         Light manufacturing and assembly of recreation equipment in enclosed buildings and which are
                  not noxious or offensive by reason of permitting odours, dust, smoke, gas, or noise.


2.    That any new buildings meet the applicable Form and Character design guidelines to the satisfaction of
      the Director of Planning prior to the issuance of a Building Permit;


3.    That, despite Section 6.13.07 and 3.16.01(1) of Zoning Bylaw No. 300, a building or structure containing
      uses permitted by this TUP may be located with a nil setback to the rear property line and high water
      mark of the ocean;

                                                                                                         July 15th, 2019
                                                                                                           Page 9 of 11


4.   That, despite, Section 6.13.05, lot coverage of all buildings and structures may not exceed 30%;


5.   That, despite, Section 6.13.06(1), no building or structure may exceed a height of three storeys;


AND that Council direct staff to meet with neighbours to address any concerns.

